---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const updated = '2026-10-22';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Cormorant has no accounts, no telemetry, and no analytics. Your browsing data stays on your devices and in your own iCloud."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1 class="font-rounded text-display font-semibold">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-caption text-muted">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated}>October 22, 2026</time>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-lead">
      Cormorant collects nothing. I can’t see what you browse, and have no way to.
    </p>

    <h2>No account</h2>
    <p>There is nothing to sign up for. Cormorant works the moment you open it.</p>

    <h2>No telemetry, no analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The app has no analytics, crash-reporting, advertising, or tracking code, and it doesn’t phone
      home. If you’ve chosen to share diagnostics with app developers in your device settings, Apple
      may pass along anonymous crash reports. That is controlled by Apple and by you.
    </p>

    <h2>Your browsing data stays with you</h2>
    <p>
      History, tabs, spaces, bookmarks, and settings are stored on your device. If you turn on sync,
      they travel through your own iCloud account, end-to-end encrypted, so only your devices can read
      them.
    </p>

    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>
      AI features stay off until you add an API key for a provider you choose. When you use one, the
      page content and your request go straight from your device to that provider, under your account
      and their terms. Nothing passes through me or is copied to me. Your keys are kept in your
      device’s Keychain.
    </p>

    <h2>The websites you visit</h2>
    <p>
      Websites can still collect data the way they would in any browser. Cormorant uses WebKit,
      including its built-in tracking prevention.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or third-party scripts.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. If this policy changes,
      the date at the top changes with it.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
